<codeline lineno="7"><highlight class="comment"><sp/>*<sp/>@section<sp/>TopMatchingSelection_intro<sp/>Introduction</highlight></codeline>
<codeline lineno="8"><highlight class="comment"><sp/>*<sp/>The<sp/>`TopMatching`<sp/>class,<sp/>implemented<sp/>in<sp/>Cython,<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>specialized<sp/>selection<sp/>template<sp/>within<sp/>the<sp/>AnalysisG<sp/>framework,<sp/>designed<sp/>for<sp/>comprehensive<sp/>analysis<sp/>of<sp/>top<sp/>quark<sp/>matching<sp/>in<sp/>Monte<sp/>Carlo<sp/>16<sp/>(MC16)<sp/>events.<sp/>It<sp/>inherits<sp/>from<sp/>the<sp/>generic<sp/>`SelectionTemplate`<sp/>class,<sp/>extending<sp/>its<sp/>functionalities<sp/>to<sp/>extract<sp/>and<sp/>organize<sp/>detailed<sp/>information<sp/>about<sp/>various<sp/>mass<sp/>definitions<sp/>(truth-level<sp/>top,<sp/>children,<sp/>truth-jets,<sp/>reconstructed<sp/>jets),<sp/>leptonicity,<sp/>and<sp/>jet<sp/>multiplicities.<sp/>This<sp/>class<sp/>facilitates<sp/>a<sp/>high-performance<sp/>extraction<sp/>and<sp/>structuring<sp/>of<sp/>top<sp/>matching<sp/>data<sp/>for<sp/>further<sp/>physics<sp/>analysis.</highlight></codeline>
